This is the git repository for the Coulomb-excitation code gosia. It is based on the original code of Tomasz Czosnyka ([homepage](https://www.pas.rochester.edu/~cline/Gosia/)).  
GOSIA is not to be confused with GOSIA2.

## Documentation
The documentation is located in the `doc` directory. It contains the GOSIA manual in different revisions.

Documentation of the internal structure of the code can be found in `internals`, including a [list of function](doc/internals/list_of_functions.txt). A pdf can be build out of the tex sources via
```bash
cd doc/internals
make all
```

More information can be found in the gosia [wiki](https://www-user.pas.rochester.edu/~gosia/mediawiki/index.php/Main_Page).

## Build
Note that in the git tree, the code is split into separate files for each function. These are combined using  
```bash
cd src
make single_file
```
Afterwards gosia can be compiled in the `src` directory with
```bash
g77 gosia_${version}.f -o gosia
```
or
```bash
gfortran gosia_${version}.f -o gosia
```

## Test
A simple test can be run with
```bash
cd simple-test
make all
```
Same can be done with the test for generating detector geometries inside the `generate-gdet-test` directory. For this test, GOSIA must be built before.
